data: {"id":"gen-1793944152-EIq4f2hKB9kwdgrL6GoL","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1793944152,"model":"openai/gpt-6-astra","provider":"OpenAI","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"","role":"assistant","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url_citation":{"url":"https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release","title":"Node.js","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"Node.js\n\nThe latest Node.js news, migration guides and events summaries\n\nReleases Node.js 27.0.0-alpha.0.0.0 (Alpha)\n\nRG\n\nRafael Gonzaga\n\nOct 29, 2026\n\nReleases Node.js 24.22.2 (LTS)\n\nADH\n\nAntoine du Hamel\n\nOct 28, 2026\n\nReleases Node.js 26.13.0 (LTS)\n\nRL\n\nRichard Lau\n\nOct 28, 2026\n\nReleases Node.js 26.12.1 (Current)\n\nADH\n\nAntoine du Hamel\n\nOct 21, 2026\n\nReleases Node.js 24.22.1 (LTS)\n\nADH\n\nAntoine du Hamel\n\nOct 21, 2026\n\nReleases Node.js 22.23.4 (LTS)\n\nAntoine du Hamel\n\nOct 21, 2026\n\nv26.13.0 Latest LTS v27.0.0-alpha.0.0.0 Latest Alpha"}}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}

data: {"id":"gen-1793944152-EIq4f2hKB9kwdgrL6GoL","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1793944152,"model":"openai/gpt-6-astra","provider":"OpenAI","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"","role":"assistant","annotations":[{"type":"url_citation","url_citation":{"url":"https://endoflife.date/nodejs","title":"Node.js | endoflife.date","start_index":0,"end_index":0,"content":"# Node.js \n\n 📅 Last updated on 29 October 2026 🤖 \n\nNode.js is an open-source, cross-platform JavaScript run-time environment built on Chrome’s V8 JavaScript engine that executes JavaScript code outside a browser.\n\n| Release | Released | Active Support | Security Support | Commercial Support | Latest |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 26 (LTS) | 6 months ago (05 May 2026) | Ends in 11 months (27 Oct 2027) | Ends in 2 years and 5 months (30 Apr 2029) | Unavailable | 26.13.0 (28 Oct 2026) |\n\n...\n\n| 24 (LTS) | 1 year and 6 months ago (06 May 2025) | Ended 2 weeks and 3 days ago (20 Oct 2026) | Ends in 1 year and 5 months (30 Apr 2028) | Unavailable | 24.22.2 (28 Oct 2026) |\n\n...\n\nMajor Node.js versions enter Current release status for six months, which gives library authors time to add support for them. After six months, releases after 26 move to Active LTS status and are ready for general use. LTS release status is “long-term support”, which typically guarantees that critical bugs will be fixed for a total of 30 months. Production applications should only use Active LTS or Maintenance LTS releases."}}]},"finish_reason":null,"native_finish_reason":null}]}

